course: dictionary
lesson: 2150
title: Copyright: who owns the work?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Copyright is a law that protects the work of people who make things. That work might be a book, a song, a picture, a film or a computer program. «Copyright is a law that protects creators' work.» The creator is the person who made the work, and they decide who can copy, sell or use it.
explain: To copyright something means to get or claim this right over it. The symbol © shows that a work is under copyright. You may also see the phrase «copyright holder», which means the person or group who owns those rights.
explain: Copyright covers more than books and songs. «Ideas and drawings belong to their makers too, which is what copyright protects.» So if you draw a picture, you are its creator, and other people need your permission before they copy it.
explain: Do not confuse copyright with plagiarism. Copyright is the law that protects a work. Plagiarism is copying someone's work and saying it's yours. In school, always give credit to the sources you use, and never pass off someone else's work as your own.
fact: Copyright is the legal right of the person who made a work to decide who can copy, sell or use it.
fact: The symbol © shows that a work is under copyright.
fact: Plagiarism means copying someone's work and saying it's yours.
fact: «Breach of copyright» means breaking the law that protects a creator's work.
fact: «Downloading songs from sites without permission breaks copyright law in most countries.»

exercise: «Copyright is a law that protects creators' work.» What does copyright protect? | *Creators' work | The weather | Money in the bank | Trees in parks
exercise: What is it called when you copy someone's work and say it's yours? | The © symbol | Out of copyright | *Plagiarism | Copyright holder
exercise: Which symbol shows that a work is under copyright? | *© | % | # | @

test: What does «breaks copyright law» mean? | Is free to do | Is a kind of song | *Goes against the law that protects the work | Makes the law stronger
test: Which phrase means the person or group who owns the rights to a work? | Breach of copyright | *Copyright holder | Plagiarism | Out of copyright

exam: Ella draws a picture, and a friend copies it without asking. Who decides who can copy the picture under copyright? | The friend, because they copied it first | The school, because it is shown there | Nobody, because pictures are free | *Ella, as the creator
